WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.131 --> 00:00:02.780
- [Narrator] When it comes
to Japanese metal work,

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:04.693
knives usually get all the glory.

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:07.357
But in the city of Sakai,

00:00:07.357 --> 00:00:09.130
where blacksmithing
goes back to the making

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:11.860
of samurai swords in the 14th century,

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:13.810
one craftsman has built a legacy

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:16.260
on something a little different.

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:21.260
Scissors to split paper, food,
and, of course, Bonsai trees.

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:33.463
This is Yasuhiro Hirakawa, who
works under the brand Sasuke.

00:00:41.085 --> 00:00:44.890
- [Narrator] Hirakawa is a
fifth generation scissor maker,

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:47.090
and he has been doing
it for half a century.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.450
He is the only traditional
scissor craftsman

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:52.713
left in all of Japan.

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:22.350
- [Narrator] It takes
Hirakawa a week or longer,

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:25.273
working 10 hours a day, to
make a pair of scissors-

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:29.360
three to four times as
long as making a knife;

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:31.923
and that effort is reflected in the price.

00:01:33.486 --> 00:01:35.819
(hammering)

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:52.300
- [Narrator] But what are you gonna do

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:54.400
with scissors that expensive?

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:55.300
To answer that,

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:59.103
here's Masakazu Yoshikawa,
a craftsman of Bonsai.

00:02:02.148 --> 00:02:05.815
(cheerful orchestral music)

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:12.560
For a master like Yoshikawa,

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.530
a key in crafting perfect Bonsai,

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:16.253
is the perfect pair of scissors.

00:03:02.856 --> 00:03:03.689
(hammering)

00:03:03.689 --> 00:03:04.522
(snipping)

00:03:04.522 --> 00:03:05.355
(hammering)

00:03:05.355 --> 00:03:06.590
- [Narrator] And Yoshikawa still remembers

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:08.723
his first pair of Sasuke scissors.

00:03:24.657 --> 00:03:26.300
(hammering)

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:27.620
- [Narrator] But for Hirakawa,

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:29.565
he's only just gotten started.

00:03:29.565 --> 00:03:31.982
(hammering)

